course: dictionary
lesson: 11850
title: Blustering: loud, boastful and empty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes a person talks very loudly and boasts a lot. They may be trying to look brave or important, perhaps because they are scared or know they are wrong. Writers call this blustering. «Toad blustered about how brave he was, but he ran from the first hiss.» The loud boasting is the clue: Toad is not really brave.
explain: Blustering can also describe weather. «The blustering wind rattled the windows all night.» Here the wind is strong and gusty, blowing hard in sudden bursts. Look at the words around it, like rattled and windows, to see that it means a strong wind, not a happy one.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If you think blustering means loud and boastful, does «The bully's blustering voice filled the playground» still make sense? It does, and it fits the idea that the bully is making noise to look powerful.
fact: Blustering means talking in a loud, boastful or angry way, often to hide that you are wrong or scared.
fact: A blustering wind is strong and gusty, blowing hard in sudden bursts.
fact: Blustering is the -ing form of the word bluster: bluster, blusters, blustered, blustering.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is blustering when he boasts and argues, and his friends see through it.
fact: A blustering king or bully makes a lot of noise but may have very little real power.
exercise: «Toad blustered about how brave he was.» What does blustered mean here? | Fell asleep under a tree | Sang a quiet song | *Talked loudly and boastfully | Walked very slowly
exercise: «The blustering wind rattled the windows all night.» What kind of wind is it? | A warm, gentle breeze | *A strong, gusty wind | A cold, still wind | A wind that makes no sound
exercise: Tom shouted, «I could beat anyone here!» then ran when the teacher came. Why might Tom be called blustering? | He was quietly reading a book | He was asleep | *He was loud and boasting to hide that he was scared | He was helping his friend
test: «The king blustered and threatened, but his army had left him.» What does this tell you about the king? | He was very tired | He was kind and quiet | *His loud talk hid that he had little real power | He had real power over everyone
test: A blustering March day means the weather is: | Foggy and still | Snowy and silent | Calm and warm | *Windy and gusty
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to blustering, when it means loud, boastful talk? | Shy | *Boastful | Gentle | Quiet
